{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nArkady wants to have a dinner. He has just returned from a shop where he has bought a semifinished cutlet. He only needs to fry it. The cutlet should be fried for 2n seconds, in particular, it should be fried for n seconds on one side and n seconds on the other side. Arkady has already got a frying pan and turn on fire, but understood that maybe he won't be able to flip the cutlet exactly after n seconds after the beginning of cooking.Arkady is too busy with sorting sticker packs in his favorite messenger and can flip the cutlet only in some periods of time. Namely, there are k periods of time in which he can do it, the i-th of them is an interval of time from li seconds after he starts cooking till ri seconds, inclusive. Arkady decided that it's not required to flip the cutlet exactly in the middle of cooking, instead, he will flip it several times in such a way that the cutlet will be fried exactly n seconds on one side and n seconds on the other side in total.Help Arkady and find out if it's possible for him to cook the cutlet, if he is able to flip the cutlet only in given periods of time; and if yes, find the minimum number of flips he needs to cook the cutlet.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 8 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n\npublic class CF939_D2_F_V5 {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Throwable {\n        MyScanner sc = new MyScanner();\n        PrintWriter pw = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n\n        int n = sc.nextInt() * 2;\n        int k = sc.nextInt();\n        int[] l = new int[k + 1];\n        int[] r = new int[k + 1];\n        SparseTable[][] seg = new SparseTable[k + 1][2];\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n            l[i] = sc.nextInt();\n            r[i] = sc.nextInt();\n        }\n        l[k] = n;\n\n        for (int j = 0; j < 2; j++) {\n            int[] a = new int[n + 2];\n            Arrays.fill(a, INF);\n            a[n / 2] = 0;\n            seg[k][j] = new SparseTable(a);\n        }\n\n        for (int i = k - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < 2; j++) {\n                int[] a = new int[n + 2];\n                Arrays.fill(a, INF);\n                for (int c = 0; c <= l[i]; c++) {\n                    int idx1 = c + l[i + 1] - l[i];\n                    int best = seg[i + 1][j].query(idx1, idx1);\n                    int idx2 = l[i + 1] - (c + r[i] - l[i]);\n                    int idx3 = l[i + 1] - c;\n                    int candidate = 1 + seg[i + 1][1 - j].query(idx2, idx3);\n                    best = Math.min(best, candidate);\n                    if (r[i] > l[i]) {\n                        int idx4 = c + 1;\n                        int idx5 = c + r[i] - l[i];\n                        candidate = 2 + seg[i + 1][j].query(idx4, idx5);\n                        best = Math.min(best, candidate);\n                    }\n                    a[c] = best;\n                }\n                seg[i][j] = new SparseTable(a);\n            }\n        }\n\n        int ans = Math.min(seg[0][0].query(l[0], l[0]), seg[0][1].query(l[0], l[0]));\n        if (ans > 2 * k) {\n            pw.println(\"Hungry\");\n        } else {\n            pw.println(\"Full\");\n            pw.println(ans);\n        }\n        pw.flush();\n        pw.close();\n    }\n\n    static final int INF = (int) 1e7;\n\n    static class SparseTable {\n        int[] arr;\n        int[][] table;\n\n        SparseTable(int[] arr) {\n            int n = arr.length;\n            this.arr = arr;\n            int k = (int) Math.floor(Math.log(n) / Math.log(2)) + 1;\n            table = new int[n][k];\n            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                table[i][0] = i;\n            }\n            for (int j = 1; (1 << j) <= n; j++) {\n                for (int i = 0; i + (1 << j) - 1 < n; i++) {\n                    int left = table[i][j - 1];\n                    int right = table[i + (1 << (j - 1))][j - 1];\n                    table[i][j] = arr[left] <= arr[right] ? left : right;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        int query(int i, int j) {\n            int len = j - i + 1;\n            int k = (int) Math.floor(Math.log(len) / Math.log(2));\n            int p1 = table[i][k];\n            int p2 = table[j - (1 << k) + 1][k];\n            return Math.min(arr[p1], arr[p2]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    static class MyScanner {\n        BufferedReader br;\n        StringTokenizer st;\n\n        public MyScanner() {\n            br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        }\n\n        String next() {\n            while (st == null || !st.hasMoreElements()) {\n                try {\n                    st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n                } catch (IOException e) {\n                    e.printStackTrace();\n                }\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n\n        long nextLong() {\n            return Long.parseLong(next());\n        }\n\n        double nextDouble() {\n            return Double.parseDouble(next());\n        }\n\n        String nextLine() {\n            String str = \"\";\n            try {\n                str = br.readLine();\n            } catch (IOException e) {\n                e.printStackTrace();\n            }\n            return str;\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n\npublic class CF939_D2_F_V5 {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Throwable {\n        MyScanner sc = new MyScanner();\n        PrintWriter pw = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        int k = sc.nextInt();\n        int[] l = new int[k + 1];\n        int[] r = new int[k + 1];\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n            l[i] = sc.nextInt();\n            r[i] = sc.nextInt();\n        }\n        l[k] = 2 * n;\n\n        // dp[i][side] = minimum flips needed starting from position i (in the i-th interval)\n        // side = 0 means we're currently frying the first side, side = 1 means second side\n        int[][] dp = new int[k + 1][2];\n        for (int i = 0; i <= k; i++) {\n            Arrays.fill(dp[i], INF);\n        }\n        \n        // Base case: at the end (position 2n), we need 0 more flips if we're in the correct state\n        dp[k][0] = 0;\n        dp[k][1] = 0;\n        \n        // Process intervals backwards\n        for (int i = k - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n            for (int side = 0; side < 2; side++) {\n                // Try not flipping in this interval\n                for (int pos = l[i]; pos <= r[i]; pos++) {\n                    int nextPos = pos + (l[i+1] - l[i]);\n                    if (nextPos <= l[i+1]) {\n                        dp[i][side] = Math.min(dp[i][side], dp[i+1][side]);\n                    }\n                }\n                \n                // Try flipping once in this interval\n                for (int pos = l[i]; pos <= r[i]; pos++) {\n                    int nextPos = pos + (l[i+1] - l[i]);\n                    if (nextPos <= l[i+1]) {\n                        dp[i][1 - side] = Math.min(dp[i][1 - side], dp[i+1][side] + 1);\n                    }\n                }\n                \n                // Try flipping twice in this interval (if interval is long enough)\n                if (r[i] - l[i] >= 1) {\n                    for (int pos1 = l[i]; pos1 <= r[i] - 1; pos1++) {\n                        for (int pos2 = pos1 + 1; pos2 <= r[i]; pos2++) {\n                            int nextPos = pos2 + (l[i+1] - l[i]);\n                            if (nextPos <= l[i+1]) {\n                                dp[i][side] = Math.min(dp[i][side], dp[i+1][side] + 2);\n                            }\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        int ans = dp[0][0];\n        if (ans >= INF / 2) {\n            pw.println(\"Hungry\");\n        } else {\n            pw.println(\"Full\");\n            pw.println(ans);\n        }\n        pw.flush();\n        pw.close();\n    }\n\n    static final int INF = (int) 1e9;\n\n    static class MyScanner {\n        BufferedReader br;\n        StringTokenizer st;\n\n        public MyScanner() {\n            br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        }\n\n        String next() {\n            while (st == null || !st.hasMoreElements()) {\n                try {\n                    st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n                } catch (IOException e) {\n                    e.printStackTrace();\n                }\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n\n        long nextLong() {\n            return Long.parseLong(next());\n        }\n\n        double nextDouble() {\n            return Double.parseDouble(next());\n        }\n\n        String nextLine() {\n            String str = \"\";\n            try {\n                str = br.readLine();\n            } catch (IOException e) {\n                e.printStackTrace();\n            }\n            return str;\n        }\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.3\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.00014804698002990335, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.95898348162882e-05, -1.6331539882230572e-05, -2.264974000354414e-06, -7.510157047363464e-06, -4.51792984677013e-05, -1.4781842764932662e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00033718624035827816, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -1.645074735279195e-05, -0.0004371640970930457, -1.5735502529423684e-05, -0.00032848684350028634, -6.079655122448457e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.003013832960277796, -5.960462772236497e-07, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -4.124556289752945e-05, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -5.5549986427649856e-05, -0.0008213722030632198, -0.00021324267436284572, -9.77468371274881e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0004316828562878072, -4.768370445162873e-07, -9.059865078597795e-06, -6.437280717364047e-06, -3.099436753473128e-06, -0.00019524575327523053, -1.645074735279195e-05, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -8.05822346592322e-05, -0.0001679517881711945, 0.0, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -0.00021944021864328533, -6.6756979322235566e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -7.617183291586116e-05, -4.410734163684538e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0001436368766007945, -4.6132929128361866e-05, 0.0, -9.536738616588991e-07, -1.0371154530730564e-05, -2.1576648578047752e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -3.838465272565372e-05, -8.583032467868179e-06, -5.4834770708112046e-05, -0.030055509880185127, -0.002358395140618086, -7.152555099310121e-07, -2.50339189733495e-06, -0.545806348323